" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An interdental brush having one or a plurality of projections (2) provided on the outer peripheral surface of a shaft (1), wherein the projections are in a fin shape and/or a hair shape and the shaft (1) and the projections (2) are integrally molded from synthetic resin, thereby it is possible to provide a soft contact with oral cavity tissues when in use, eliminate variations in coming-off strength of fin- and hair-shape projections, and reduce production costs.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette brosse interdentaire comporte au moins une branche (2) prenant naissance sur la surface périphérique externe d'un axe (1). Ces branches présentent la forme d'une ailette et/ou d'un poil. L'axe (1) et les branches (2) sont moulés d'un seul tenant en résine de synthèse. Cela permet, d'une part de réaliser, à l'utilisation, un contact doux avec les tissus de la cavité orale, et d'autre part de réduire les coûts de production.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>